    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d439">

                <pb facs="0576" n="508" sameAs="frus:frus1867p1/pg508"/>

                <head>Mr. Seward to Mr.
                        Burlingame</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 216]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <hi
                                rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1867-09-20"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >September</hi> 20, 1867.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I transmit for your information a copy of a
                        despatch,<anchor n="*" xml:id="d439-f1"/> and of its accompaniments, of the
                    26th of July last, No. 109, from General Dix, our minister at Paris, in relation
                    to the municipal regulations proposed to be adopted by the French consul general
                    at Shanghai. A copy of my reply is also enclosed.</p>
                <p>I am, sir, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>WILLIAM H. SEWARD.</signed>
                </closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Anson Burlingame</hi>, Esq., <hi
                            rendition="#italic">&amp;c., &amp;c., &amp;c.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d439-f1" n="*" xml:id="d439-f1-content">
                <p>For enclosures see correspondence with United States minister at Paris.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
